gthr: add a thread model over ISO C11 <threads.h>, --enable-threads=c11

libgcc and libstdc++ reach threads only through gthr.h, which includes the
header of the target's thread model. GCC has none over the C11 thread functions
(thrd_create, mtx_lock, cnd_wait, tss_create, call_once), so a bare-metal target
with a C library that has them can only configure --enable-threads=no, which makes
every mutex a no-op and leaves libstdc++ without std::thread, std::mutex,
std::condition_variable, std::future and the rest of <thread> and <mutex>.

libgcc/gthr-c11.h is the thread model. C11 has no static initializers for
mutexes and condition variables, so it defines __GTHREAD_MUTEX_INIT_FUNCTION,
__GTHREAD_RECURSIVE_MUTEX_INIT_FUNCTION and __GTHREAD_COND_INIT_FUNCTION and not
__GTHREAD_MUTEX_INIT and friends; a thread's start routine returns an int, so
__gthread_create starts the thread through a small heap record that holds the
void * routine and its argument; every mutex is initialized as mtx_timed so it
can be locked with a timeout; and the results are the errno values the POSIX
functions return. There is no read-write lock, so libstdc++ uses its own.

The model is named in gcc/configure.ac (the list of valid --enable-threads
values) and in GCC_AC_THREAD_HEADER (config/gthr.m4), which libgcc and
libstdc++ use to find the header. The generated configure scripts of gcc, libgcc
and libstdc++-v3 are edited the same way, so no autoconf run is needed.

diff -ruN a/config/gthr.m4 b/config/gthr.m4
--- a/config/gthr.m4
+++ b/config/gthr.m4
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 [
 case $1 in
     aix)	thread_header=config/rs6000/gthr-aix.h ;;
+    c11)	thread_header=gthr-c11.h ;;
     dce)	thread_header=config/pa/gthr-dce.h ;;
     gcn)	thread_header=config/gcn/gthr-gcn.h ;;
     lynx)	thread_header=config/gthr-lynx.h ;;
diff -ruN a/gcc/configure b/gcc/configure
--- a/gcc/configure
+++ b/gcc/configure
@@ -13220,7 +13220,7 @@
     target_thread_file='single'
     ;;
   aix | dce | lynx | mipssde | posix | rtems | \
-  single | tpf | vxworks | win32 | mcf)
+  single | tpf | vxworks | win32 | mcf | c11)
     target_thread_file=${enable_threads}
     ;;
   *)
diff -ruN a/gcc/configure.ac b/gcc/configure.ac
--- a/gcc/configure.ac
+++ b/gcc/configure.ac
@@ -2110,7 +2110,7 @@
     target_thread_file='single'
     ;;
   aix | dce | lynx | mipssde | posix | rtems | \
-  single | tpf | vxworks | win32 | mcf)
+  single | tpf | vxworks | win32 | mcf | c11)
     target_thread_file=${enable_threads}
     ;;
   *)
diff -ruN a/libgcc/configure b/libgcc/configure
--- a/libgcc/configure
+++ b/libgcc/configure
@@ -5816,6 +5816,7 @@
 
 case $target_thread_file in
